armada — one vocabulary for a repo's stack, and the agents working in it

USAGE
  armada <module> <verb> [flags]  the verbs Armada owns
  armada                          enter Helm, the agent you talk to

MANIFEST — what a workspace is and how to operate it
  config <scan|verify>  report the evidence, then verify what was written
  init                  claim this workspace: ports, .armada/, setup
  up [<component>]      start this workspace's services; wait until they answer
  down [<component>]    stop this workspace's services; keep the port block
  status                what is running, what is mine, what is stale
  check [<selector>]    lint, format and test — the verb a gate calls
  skills [show <name>]  what this repository knows about itself
  clean                 release what this workspace owns
  <name>                a commands: entry from this repo's armada.yml

GUILD — you, portable: voice, skills, hooks, workflows
  init             build your guild by interviewing you
  pull             bring this machine's guild up to date
  push             send local guild changes to the remote
  export           write the whole guild to one portable file
  import <bundle>  restore a guild from a bundle

FLEET — the agents you do not talk to: Jobs, worktrees, budgets
  spawn <task>           start an isolated agent Job on a task
  ls                     what is running, what it has spent, and who needs you
  board <job>            take a Job over yourself: worktree and resume command
  answer <job> <answer>  give a waiting Job your decision; let it continue
  inbox                  what the fleet needs from you
  kill [<job>]           end a Job and release everything it owns

THIS MACHINE
  init    set up this machine: checks, ~/.armada/, and your guild
  doctor  what this machine is missing, and what fixes it

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --json          answer as one JSON object, for a script or an agent
  --color <when>  auto (default), always, never; NO_COLOR wins
  -h, --help      this page, or a verb's own flags
  -V, --version   the version

NOT BUILT YET
  armada helm, bridge                         M3
  armada guild edit, verify                   M2
  armada manifest render, agents-md, explain  reserved
  armada manifest check --detach, --status    reserved

  Each is claimed and answers `not built yet`, so that a name which is
  going to mean one thing never means something else first.

Run `armada <module> <verb> --help` for a verb's own flags.

Global flags come before the module. Everything after a commands: name is the
child's, including flags Armada itself defines.
